## 2026-06-24 — Sprint 10 / Sprint 11 Sequencing Swap: Agent Routing Before Learning

**Date:** 2026-06-24

**Decision:**
Switch Sprint 10 and Sprint 11.
- Sprint 10 becomes Agent / Capability Routing + Useful Tool Foundation.
- Sprint 11 becomes Learning / Preference Adaptation.

**Reason:**
Learning/adaptation must not train on unstable general-planner/tool-selection behavior. Agent/capability routing and useful tool boundaries must stabilize first so learning is based on validated successful routes, tools, and capability outcomes.

Bad learning risks to record:
- learning false-success final answers as acceptable
- learning stale file/web tool choices for math final answers
- learning over-specific global compiler patches as preferred behavior
- learning ambiguous plural-reference guesses
- learning local LLM variance artifacts
- learning bad planner/tool-selection routes as successful

**New sequence:**
- Sprint 10 — Agent / Capability Routing + Useful Tool Foundation
- Sprint 11 — Learning / Preference Adaptation
- Sprint 12 — Plan Control + Workflow Repair UX
- Sprint 13 — Privacy / Local-First Enforcement + Operator UX
- Sprint 14 — Sandbox / Self-Improvement Design Milestone

**Explicitly not introduced:**
- no learning activation in Sprint 10
- no broad multi-agent authority
- no lifecycle/governance/system_entry authority change
- no adaptive orchestration activation
- no prompt change by this documentation update

**Status:** ROADMAP UPDATED / IMPLEMENTATION NOT STARTED

