## 2026-06-08 — Optional Budget-Guarded OpenRouter LLM Routing and Workflow-Linked LLM Observability

**Date:** 2026-06-08

**Decision:**
Adopt optional role-based cloud LLM routing through OpenRouter as a local-first performance/quality enhancement.

Keep default posture local/Ollama.

OpenRouter may be used only when configured by backend environment and selected through runtime settings.

OpenRouter key must be read from backend environment variable only:
MH_OPENROUTER_API_KEY

GUI must not display, edit, transmit back to frontend state, or write the API key to .env.

Runtime settings may be adjusted through GUI, but in-memory only for this phase.

MutesHand budget guard remains separate from OpenRouter key/account limit.

LLM provider/model observability must be recorded in an append-only local usage ledger.

LLM observability may be displayed globally in LLM Settings and per-workflow in History, but remains read-only.

Workflow-linked LLM calls may be shown in History through sanitized usage endpoints.

LLM observability data must not influence lifecycle, governance, retry, projection, memory, or execution control flow.

**Reason:**
PERF-036 measured LLM latency as the dominant performance bottleneck.

Timeout/circuit breaker implementation was rejected and reverted because it caused GUI/runtime regressions.

Removing planner/AG1/formatter calls was rejected as behavior-changing.

Optional OpenRouter routing allows testing faster/free cloud models without forcing cloud use.

Budget and key visibility are required so the operator can safely experiment without unexpected spend.

Workflow-linked LLM observability is needed to debug model/provider behavior after execution, especially planner behavior.

History is the safest long-term destination for per-workflow LLM calls because it is read-only inspection, not lifecycle authority.

**Architectural Clarifications:**
OpenRouter is optional, not a default authority.

Ollama/local remains the reset/default posture.

Provider routing is utility infrastructure below orchestration authority.

execute_llm return shape remains unchanged.

LLM provider/model selection does not alter lifecycle authority.

LLM budget/usage ledger is append-only observability only.

History LLM Calls is read-only inspection.

Projection must not include LLM observability as authority.

Frontend must not infer lifecycle or retry legality from LLM telemetry.

MutesHand budget guard is local/estimated and separate from OpenRouter account/key limits.

OpenRouter free models may still be rate-limited even when estimated cost is zero.

Workflow_id linkage is passive correlation, not lifecycle authority.

**Verified Outcomes:**
OpenRouter provider routing implemented.

Per-role provider routing implemented for planner/agent/formatter/validator roles.

Free-model pools implemented.

OpenRouter model catalogue refresh implemented and manually validated.

OpenRouter key/account refresh implemented and manually validated.

LLM Settings GUI implemented with mode/provider controls, model pool controls, free-model selector, MutesHand budget guard, OpenRouter key/account status, and Recent LLM Calls.

Recent LLM Calls now shows concrete provider/model/status/route/cost.

Usage ledger records concrete OpenRouter model IDs.

Intentional Ollama calls are not marked as fallback.

Planner OpenRouter routing manually validated.

AG1/formatter local Ollama routing preserved.

GET /llm/usage/workflow/{workflow_id} implemented.

HistoryInspector LLM Calls section implemented.

Manual validation confirmed History LLM Calls shows:
- planner / openrouter / concrete free model / success / role_provider_openrouter
- ag1_tool_selection / ollama / llama3.1:8b / success / role_provider_ollama

**Explicitly NOT Introduced:**
- no timeout/circuit breaker reintroduced
- no execute_llm return-shape change
- no planner/AG1/formatter removal
- no lifecycle authority change
- no governance authority change
- no projection authority change
- no retry/recovery change
- no memory authority change
- no API key exposure
- no .env writes
- no projection-carried LLM authority
- no frontend lifecycle synthesis
- no LLM telemetry control-flow dependency
- no live/in-flight planner LLM visibility in this phase
- no planner_llm_started / planner_llm_completed event-bus events
- no formatter workflow_id linkage
- no validator workflow_id linkage

**Impact:**
AI Lab can now safely test optional cloud/free LLM models while retaining local-first defaults.

Operator can inspect budget/account state and model/provider routing from the GUI.

Operator can inspect per-workflow planner/AG1 LLM calls from History.

LLM routing observability is materially improved without authority drift.

Future live/in-flight planner visibility remains a separate deferred UX/observability issue.

**Status:** COMPLETE + MANUALLY VALIDATED — OPTIONAL LOCAL-FIRST CLOUD ROUTING / READ-ONLY LLM OBSERVABILITY

