**Decision:** Formalize architectural separation between passive observability visibility and runtime authority ownership.

**Reason:** Dashboard/discovery architecture clarification required explicit prevention of frontend authority synthesis and observability-derived orchestration control assumptions.

**Verified Rules:**
- Visibility does NOT imply authority
- Dashboard/discovery layers are passive observability only
- Focused workflow screens are explicit attachment surfaces
- Frontend remains projection-derived only
- Websocket/event transport layers remain non-authoritative
- Runtime truth supersedes projection interpretation

**Impact:**
