## 2026-06-07 — OPERATIONAL_ROADMAP_V2 Approval and V1 Supersession

**Date:** 2026-06-07

**Decision:**
OPERATIONAL_ROADMAP_V2.txt is approved as the active operational roadmap authority after SA / Product Owner review following the completed Functional Product Gap Audit, Risk Audit, Performance Audit, and Production/Platform Audit.
OPERATIONAL_ROADMAP_V1.txt and OPERATIONAL_ROADMAP_SUMMARY_V1.txt are superseded and must not be used for active operational execution.

**Reason:**
V1 correctly stabilized the core runtime and stopped architecture drift through Sprint 6. However, V1 allowed architecture stabilization and operational hardening to become the primary execution path while the product-facing intelligence layer — memory activation, learning/adaptation, agent expansion, approval UX, user override, privacy enforcement — remained functionally incomplete.
The audits proved the system is architecturally aligned but at roughly 22% SYSTEM_GOALS_V2 functional completion. V2 rebalances the roadmap center of gravity toward product capability.

**V2 Key Changes:**
- Product capability activation is the primary roadmap line (Sprints 7–12)
- Memory advisory activation (Sprint 7) is the first product capability milestone
- PERF-036 trivial-prompt latency measurement is a P0 usability gate before Sprint 7 capability claims
- GUI approval surface, notifications, and user override/force-execution design are Sprint 7 scope
- Learning / preference adaptation sequenced to Sprint 8
- Agent and tool expansion sequenced to Sprint 9
- Plan control / workflow repair sequenced to Sprint 10
- Privacy and local-first data enforcement sequenced to Sprint 11
- Production hardening is a bounded parallel safety/platform track, not the primary sprint
- P0 hardening items (CORS, admin gating, /health endpoint) are allowed in Sprint 7 only where they prevent unsafe use or block product evaluation

**Architecture Preservation:**
All frozen architecture rules remain unchanged:
- deterministic runtime authority
- governance supremacy
- centralized orchestration topology
