## 2026-06-07 — ADOPT-005A Odysseus Tool Catalogue Audit + Licensing Attribution Policy

**Date:** 2026-06-07

**Decision:**
Complete audit of Odysseus tool catalogue and establish formal licensing/attribution policy for all future Odysseus-derived code in AI Lab.

**Audit Deliverable:**
`E:\MutesHand\Project Docs\ODYSSEUS_TOOL_CATALOGUE_AND_LICENSING_AUDIT_V1.md`

**Audit Scope:**
- 84 tools/capabilities identified across schemas, security, policy, MCP, search, research, memory, and skill modules
- Classifications: 3 COPY WITH NOTICE, 8 ADAPT UTILITY, 14 IDEA ONLY, 28 AVOID, 17 SA ESCALATION, 14 infrastructure modules

**Key Finding:**
Odysseus is MIT-licensed and feature-rich, but its core architecture (agent loop owns tool execution) is fundamentally incompatible with AI Lab's governance-owned execution model via `system_entry`. Most high-value items require AI Lab-native rewrite, not direct copy.

**Licensing / Attribution Policy Established:**
1. All Odysseus-derived code must carry MIT attribution in module docstring
2. Attribution format: source file path, original copyright, modification description
3. Direct copy is permitted ONLY for small standalone deterministic utilities (COPY WITH NOTICE)
4. ADAPT UTILITY items must be rewritten for AI Lab style; attribution still required
5. IDEA ONLY items require no attribution (concepts, prompts, design patterns)
6. AVOID and SA ESCALATION items must not be copied under any circumstance
7. No Odysseus runtime code (`tool_execution.py`, `agent_loop.py`, `agent_tools.py`) may be copied

**Architecture Boundary Confirmation:**
- Tool execution must remain governance-owned via `system_entry`
- No agent-loop tool dispatchers may be introduced
- No MCP runtime without SA escalation and security audit
- No shell/python execution without sandboxing architecture
- Projection/frontend remains non-authoritative (no `ui_control` equivalent)

**Status:** COMPLETE — ADOPT-005A audit delivered; policy active for all future Odysseus adoption work

