**Decision:**
Sprint 8 is closed as COMPLETE for the current approved PDIAG-006 modernization/evaluation scope. All approved items (PDIAG-001 through PDIAG-006, RS1, PC1, Prompt V2 promotion, EVAL1 P0/P1/P2, E.7 classification, CL1 cloud comparison) are validated and accepted. Staged planner is not justified by current evidence. Broader P1 cloud comparison remains optional, not required. Document-intelligence planning (PDIAG-007), optional dependency/partial-failure semantics (PDIAG-008-LEGACY), and abstract-resource sequencing remain deferred for future Head Dev/SA design.

*(Superseded by revised decision below: Sprint 8 remains open due to ISSUE-PDIAG-008 spike.)*

**Reason:**
Planner / DAG / final-output diagnostic identified structural gaps that were systematically addressed through the approved PDIAG-006 scope. Local P0 baseline now passes 30/30 with 17/17 critical gates. Cloud P0 baseline (OpenRouter `openrouter/owl-alpha`) also passes 30/30 with 17/17 critical gates. Evaluation harness now contains 103 implemented cases. The evidence does not justify a staged planner architecture at this time.

**What was completed:**
- PDIAG-001: Multi-reference dependency extraction + partial dependency validation — IMPLEMENTED + VALIDATED
- PDIAG-002: Final synthesis dependency binding (validator fail-safe + planning compiler auto-binding) — IMPLEMENTED + VALIDATED
- PDIAG-003: SAME retry no-prior-tool handling (retry budget guard) — IMPLEMENTED + VALIDATED
- PDIAG-004: Workflow output aggregation / final result assembly — IMPLEMENTED + VALIDATED
- PDIAG-005 Phase 1: Advisory-only false-success detection — IMPLEMENTED + VALIDATED
- PDIAG-005 Phase 2A: Narrow `purpose_met` governance hook for `unresolved_placeholder` and `instruction_echo_output` — IMPLEMENTED + VALIDATED
- PDIAG-006 AG1/tool-index/F1: Canonical tool manifest + AG1 capability grounding + dependency-output purpose enrichment — IMPLEMENTED + VALIDATED

