## 2026-06-20 — Sprint 8 Closure REVISED: Sprint 8 Remains Open (ISSUE-PDIAG-008 Spike)

**Decision:**
Sprint 8 closure is REVISED. Sprint 8 is NOT CLOSED. PDIAG-006 approved scope remains complete and validated. Sprint 8 remains open because manual GUI validation discovered new AG1 tool-selection regressions (ISSUE-PDIAG-008) that were not caught by the 103-case evaluation harness.

**Scope of active spike:**
- ISSUE-PDIAG-008A: Final-answer steps selecting unrelated tools (e.g., `square_root`) instead of `finalize_output`, producing wrong successful output.
- ISSUE-PDIAG-008B: Local LLM file write/create `argument_count_mismatch` failure.

**Reason:**
Bad successful final answers can pollute Sprint 11 learning/adaptation evidence and Sprint 9 live observability testability. Local file write reliability matters for local-first evidence workflows. Sprint 8 will not close until PDIAG-008 is audited, classified, and resolved or accepted.

**Consequences:**
- Sprint 9 was originally planned as Learning / Preference Adaptation; this was later reframed as Live Observability / Streaming / Testability per 2026-06-20 Roadmap Direction Change decision.
- Sprint 9 — Live Observability / Streaming / Testability is NOT opened until PDIAG-008 is resolved or accepted as a precondition.
- No implementation of PDIAG-008 fixes until audit findings are returned and reviewed.
- All items previously listed as "deferred" from Sprint 7/8 have been moved to specific future sprint or track ownership in OPERATIONAL_ROADMAP_V3.txt Section 8.5. No loose deferred piles remain.

**Status:** ACTIVE SPIKE / PENDING AUDIT

