## 2026-06-20 — Roadmap Direction Change: Sprint 9 Reframed as Live Observability / Streaming / Testability

**Decision:**
After Sprint 8 PDIAG-006 approved scope completion, Head Dev Bryan selected a revised roadmap sequence:
1. Post-Sprint-8 Small Tech-Debt Closeout (bounded, small, low-risk items only)
2. Sprint 9 — Live Observability / Streaming / Testability (NOT OPENED until PDIAG-008 resolved)
3. Sprint 10 — Agent / Capability Routing + Useful Tool Foundation (moved from Sprint 11 position per 2026-06-24 sequencing swap)

**Reason:**
Learning/adaptation must not train on unstable general-planner/tool-selection behavior. Agent/capability routing and useful tool boundaries must stabilize first so learning is based on validated successful routes, tools, and capability outcomes. Sprint 9 live observability and streaming infrastructure is a product capability enabler that should precede both tracks. Small tech-debt closeout after Sprint 8 prevents deferred hardening items from accumulating.

**What changed:**
- Sprint 9 renamed from "Learning / Preference Adaptation" to "Live Observability / Streaming / Testability"
- Agent / Capability Routing + Useful Tool Foundation moved to Sprint 10
- Learning / Preference Adaptation moved to Sprint 11
- Plan Control + Workflow Repair moved to Sprint 12
- Privacy / Local-First Enforcement moved to Sprint 13
- Sandbox / Self-Improvement Design Milestone moved to Sprint 14
- Post-Sprint-8 Small Tech-Debt Closeout added as explicit planned phase between Sprint 8 and Sprint 9

**Specific item reclassifications:**
- `/health` and `/ready` endpoints → Post-Sprint-8 Small Tech-Debt Closeout
- CORS restriction → deferred until phone/LAN/dev-device access model is defined
- Task Hub small UX cleanup → late UX polish, not small cleanup
- WebSockets/live streaming → planned for Sprint 9, bounded to hints/status/observability; full projection delivery requires SA approval
- Live / in-flight planner LLM visibility → Sprint 9 core scope
- Formatter/validator workflow-linked LLM observability → optional small cleanup or Sprint 9 candidate

**Consequences:**
- Sprint 9 will not open until PDIAG-008 is resolved or accepted.
- WebSocket implementation is planned but bounded; architecture guardrails preserved.
- Polling fallback remains mandatory.
- Canonical projection endpoint remains projection truth.

**Status:** RECORDED

